{:id "0045-lab-gestures"
 :title "Lab gestures: every effect becomes a patch (data), eight new gestures join, and 'loooove' swells like a held note"
 :lupa/deps #{"0042-lab-synth"}
 :lupa/area :lab
 :lupa/risk :medium
 :goal "docs/product/score.md and hypothesis H1 in
        docs/product/lab-notebook.md: one small synthesizer can express
        every effect the lab has. Replace lab.pose's hand-written
        effect-delta with patches played by lab.synth, prove the eleven
        old effects move exactly as before, add the eight new gestures the
        foreman specified, and make the first subtle read: a word with a
        held letter ('loooove') swells, each letter lifting in turn, as
        Ben measured in the Music app's lyrics."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/lab/gestures.cljc" "test/halfahead/lab/gestures_test.cljc"
         "src/halfahead/lab/pose.cljc" "test/halfahead/lab/pose_test.cljc"
         "src/halfahead/lab/cues.cljc" "test/halfahead/lab/cues_test.cljc"
         "src/halfahead/lab/glossary.cljc" "e2e/lab.mjs" "docs/LAB.md"]
 :design "halfahead.lab.gestures (.cljc, data): patches, a map from every
          :ha/word-effect to a :ha/patch, and (patch effect).
          The eleven existing effects, transcribed from lab.pose's
          effect-delta, effect-ms and stagger so they move exactly as
          today. All have :stagger {:ms-per-glyph 25 :max-ms 100};
          :rewind's is :order :reverse. For example :melt is {:ms 1400
          :mods [{:channel :y :amount -0.4 :curve :rise-sine :from 0 :to
          3/7} {:channel :rx :amount 0.6 :curve :rise-sine :from 0 :to 3/7}
          {:channel :y :amount -0.4 :curve :fade2 :from 3/7 :to 1 :osc
          {:wave :cosine :period-ms 1600/3}} {:channel :rx :amount 0.6
          ...the same...}]} (as doubles); :fuse uses :each :even/:odd for
          z (0.6 and 0.3) and :alternate? for y; the jittering ones use
          :osc with :phase :id and the salts effect-delta uses.
          Proof (H1): move today's effect-delta and effect-ms, unchanged,
          into gestures_test.cljc as the reference, and assert that for
          each of the eleven, (synth/delta (patch e) u i n id k) equals the
          reference within 1e-9 on every channel, for u on a 7 ms grid over
          the effect's duration, positions 0 to 5, ids 0, 3 and 11, k 0.3
          and 1. If one cannot be matched, do not bend the others: say
          which and why at the top of the final message.
          The eight new gestures, exactly these (amounts at intensity 1):
            :swell  {:ms 2400 :stagger {:ms-per-glyph 120 :max-ms 900}
                     :mods [{:channel :y :amount 0.25 :curve :rise-sine :from 0 :to 0.375}
                            {:channel :y :amount 0.25 :curve :fade2 :from 0.375 :to 1}
                            {:channel :glow :amount 0.45 :curve :arch}]}
            :bloom  {:ms 1600 :stagger {:ms-per-glyph 40 :max-ms 200}
                     :mods [{:channel :weight :amount 0.6 :curve :arch}
                            {:channel :glow :amount 0.5 :curve :arch}
                            {:channel :scale :amount 0.06 :curve :arch}]}
            :slam   {:ms 900 :stagger {:ms-per-glyph 15 :max-ms 60}
                     :mods [{:channel :scale :amount 1.4 :curve :spring-fall}
                            {:channel :z :amount 2.0 :curve :spring-fall}
                            {:channel :weight :amount 0.8 :curve :fade2}
                            {:channel :glow :amount 0.7 :curve :fade2}]}
            :hush   {:ms 1400 :stagger {:ms-per-glyph 20 :max-ms 100}
                     :mods [{:channel :scale :amount -0.12 :curve :arch}
                            {:channel :weight :amount -0.5 :curve :arch}
                            {:channel :blur :amount 0.35 :curve :arch}
                            {:channel :opacity :amount -0.3 :curve :arch}]}
            :lean   {:ms 1300 :stagger {:ms-per-glyph 30 :max-ms 150}
                     :mods [{:channel :skew :amount 0.28 :curve :rise :from 0 :to 0.3}
                            {:channel :skew :amount 0.28 :curve :fall :from 0.3 :to 1}]}
            :nod    {:ms 700 :stagger {:ms-per-glyph 20 :max-ms 100}
                     :mods [{:channel :y :amount -0.12 :curve :arch}
                            {:channel :rx :amount 0.25 :curve :arch}]}
            :shiver {:ms 1100
                     :mods [{:channel :x :amount 0.035 :curve :fade
                             :osc {:wave :sine :period-ms 55 :phase :id :salt 6}}
                            {:channel :blur :amount 0.25 :curve :fade2}]}
            :draw   {:ms 500
                     :mods [{:channel :fill :amount -1.0 :curve :fall}
                            {:channel :glow :amount 0.3 :curve :arch}]}
          gestures tests: every :ha/word-effect has a patch; every patch
          has no synth/problems; (synth/total-ms p 40) x 1.5 (the slowest
          tempo) <= 5000 for each.
          lab.pose: cue-deltas plays (gestures/patch effect) through
          lab.synth in place of effect-delta, effect-ms and stagger-step
          (delete them): each letter's start is (synth/start-ms patch i n)
          x tempo, its delta (synth/delta patch (cue-ms u ms ps) i n id k),
          then styled by performed as now. A style's :amplitude also
          scales :sx :sy and :skew. apply-deltas learns the new channels:
          :sx and :sy rest at 1 (a delta adds to 1, never below 0), :skew
          at 0, :weight at 0 kept in [-1 1], :blur at 0 in [0 1], :fill at
          1 in [0 1]; a :tint delta is dropped (nothing gives letters an
          ink yet). A pose carries one of these keys only when its value
          differs from rest, so every existing frame is unchanged. Cues
          now settle within 5000 ms of their cause in every style (was
          2500); births, ghosts, shots and every other invariant are as
          they were. Update the namespace doc and the settle tests to say
          so, and keep every other pose test passing unchanged.
          lab.cues: a word with one letter three or more times in a row
          (compare case-insensitively; letters only) is a held word: its
          cue is {:effect :swell :intensity (min 1 (+ 0.5 (* 0.1 (- run
          2)))) :source :elongation}. Order of rules: glossary,
          elongation, punctuation, shape, default.
          lab.glossary: after \"wobble\", add the eight new gestures
          performing their own names, each at intensity 0.9, under a
          comment dated 2026-11-17: \"swell\" \"bloom\" \"slam\" \"hush\"
          \"lean\" \"nod\" \"shiver\" \"draw\". Change nothing else there.
          e2e/lab.mjs, one new step 'swell' (with ?debug&reveal=3, and
          the Plain style picked first, so no style adds sway): type
          'I loooove it '; the overlay shows 'loooove -> swell 0.7
          (elongation)'; sample window.__lab's frame on every animation
          frame for 6 s and assert, independent of frame rate: at least
          one sampled frame has a letter of 'loooove' lifted above its
          resting y; no sampled lift exceeds 0.25 x 0.7 + 0.001 em; the
          peak lift of each letter of the word
          comes no earlier than the letter before it (among frames
          sampled); and 5.5 s after the cue every letter is at rest.
          Screenshot out/lab/swell.png about 1 s after the cue.
          docs/LAB.md: a section 'Gestures and patches' (what a patch is,
          the table of nineteen gestures, how to add one, that
          synth/problems is the gate), and the settle time."
 :acceptance
 ["gestures tests: the H1 equivalence for all eleven old effects (or an
   honest list of those that could not be matched), the eight new patches
   exactly as specified, no problems, within the cap; the eight glossary
   entries"
  "pose and cues tests updated as in the design; all other existing tests
   pass unchanged"
  "`bb lab:e2e` passes with the swell step and every existing step; `bb
   test` stays green; out/lab/swell.png for the foreman"]
 :non-goals
 ["No renderer changes: the new channels (:weight :blur :skew :fill :sx
   :sy) reach the frame as data and are drawn by a later order"
  "No changes to lab.synth, styles, the director, sound, reveal or the
   stage, and none to the glossary beyond the eight entries; do not edit
   the schema"
  "Do not run `bb e2e` or `bb play`"]
 :context ["docs/product/score.md" "docs/product/lab-notebook.md"
           "src/halfahead/schema.cljc" "src/halfahead/lab/synth.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/lab/pose.cljc" "test/halfahead/lab/pose_test.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/lab/cues.cljc" "e2e/lab.mjs" "docs/LAB.md" "DESIGN.md"]
 :budget-usd 12.0}
